 \fB\-\-save\-downloads\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR
 If files are downloaded, save them to \fIDIRECTORY\fR.
 .TP
+\fB\-\-progress\-fd\fR \fIFD\fR
+Write machine-readable progress to file descriptor \fIFD\fR, one line per
+event:
+.BI "step " text
+(what is being done),
+.BI "file " "name bytes"
+(a file being checked or unpacked),
+.BI "generated " path
+(a package was built) and, once before a failed run exits,
+.BI "error " "kind text"
+with \fIkind\fR one of
+.BR not\-found ,
+.BR unknown\-version ,
+.BR unsuitable ,
+.BR needs\-download ,
+.B no\-space
+or
+.BR failed .
+The normal output is unchanged.
+.TP
 .B \-\-verbose
 Be more verbose, and in particular show output from any external tools
 that are invoked during operation.
